      "writtenOn": "2017-03-20T23:13:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think the BluetoothHci object is ever destructed, and the lifetime of BluetoothDeathRecipient is tied to the lifetime of the BLuetoothHci object. So there\u0027s not really a need to set this to nullptr. In fact if you would, I don\u0027t think it would ever get set correctly again.",
