    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "504e22f5_e3e648e6",
        "filename": "bluetooth/1.0/default/bluetooth_hci.cc",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 1013030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-20T23:13:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It depends if VendorInterface::Shutdown() is resilient against being called multiple times (without an open() in-between). What could happen if you move it down is:\n1) com.android.bluetooth calls close()\n2) VendorInterface::Shutdown() is running (let\u0027s say it takes a while)\n3) meanwhile, com.android.bluetooth dies\n4) death recipient runs on another hwbinder thread, and calls close() again.\n\nIt looks like you have only one hwbinder thread though, and then this can\u0027t really happen, as death recipients are run on the same hwbinder thread close() would have come in on. So in this case, I don\u0027t think it matters.",
      "parentUuid": "21afed89_d1160261",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 112,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 31
      },
